      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-20-826",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "001568acae4c23a705c80c0204aa229ca392bb942e06d03d2fc99c98e8ec8c88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-001568acae4c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Davenport's concession that Brecht doesn't always subsume AEDPA narrows the dispute here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-826",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "001568acae4c23a705c80c0204aa229ca392bb942e06d03d2fc99c98e8ec8c88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-001568acae4c-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Ms. Hammoud, do we have to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2021-20-826",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "001568acae4c23a705c80c0204aa229ca392bb942e06d03d2fc99c98e8ec8c88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-001568acae4c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Has there ever been a case where a court granted relief under Brecht and then said, sorry, we can't grant relief because of AEDPA/Chapman?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice THOMAS",
      "case_id": "2021-20-826",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "001568acae4c23a705c80c0204aa229ca392bb942e06d03d2fc99c98e8ec8c88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-001568acae4c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I understand that, but if you had to choose between one or the other, which has the higher status?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Bahal",
      "case_id": "2021-20-826",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "001568acae4c23a705c80c0204aa229ca392bb942e06d03d2fc99c98e8ec8c88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-001568acae4c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BAHAL: Thank you, Justice Kavanaugh. This Court has made clear, first in Holbrook and again in Deck, that relying on juror testimony as to whether the effect of shackles affected their verdict is unreliable because a juror will not always be aware of the effect of seeing a defendant in shackles."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-826",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "001568acae4c23a705c80c0204aa229ca392bb942e06d03d2fc99c98e8ec8c88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-001568acae4c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: You mentioned that the Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-826",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "001568acae4c23a705c80c0204aa229ca392bb942e06d03d2fc99c98e8ec8c88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-001568acae4c-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Rebuttal, Ms. HAMMOUD?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-826",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "001568acae4c23a705c80c0204aa229ca392bb942e06d03d2fc99c98e8ec8c88",
      "evidence_id": "ev-001568acae4c-0002-0005",
